From: Stephender (Antigravity Phase 2, Fix 5 — packaging & binary trim)
Subject: [PATCH] Trim packaging bloat and enable Release dead-section elimination

Phase 2 Fix 5 from ANTIGRAVITY-PLAN.md. Applies cleanly on top of
0001-undo-hardening + 0002-physical-ram + 0003-ram-aware-cache +
0004-tbb-trim-thp-guard + 0005-startup-ram-lazy-loading against
Blender v5.2.4 (cd5dc428cce1).

100% of features preserved. No add-ons, locales, Cycles GPU kernels
(5.2/scripts/addons_core/cycles/lib/* or lib/libcycles_kernel_oneapi_aot.so),
or Python docstrings (-OO) are removed or altered.

Summary of changes
------------------
1. source/creator/CMakeLists.txt (Python install exclusions):
   - Linux/Unix `install_dir()` and system-Python fallback:
     Upstream `PATTERN "config-${PYTHON_VERSION}/*.a" EXCLUDE` missed both
     multiarch config directories (`config-3.13-x86_64-linux-gnu/libpython3.13.a`,
     84,181,888 bytes) and the top-level copy (`lib/libpython3.13.a`,
     84,181,888 bytes). Update to `PATTERN "config-${PYTHON_VERSION}*/*.a" EXCLUDE`
     and `PATTERN "libpython*.a" EXCLUDE`.
     Measured saving on fix4-linux: -168,363,776 bytes (-160.56 MiB).
     Preserves numpy's small static libs (126 KB) and all Python runtime files.
   - Windows Release/RelWithDebInfo/MinSizeRel Python `lib` install:
     Add `PATTERN "*.pdb" EXCLUDE` (matching the existing `DLLs` install rule
     directly below it) to exclude `venvlauncher.pdb` (3,829,760 bytes) and
     `venvwlauncher.pdb` (3,846,144 bytes). Debug config is untouched.
     Measured saving on fix4-windows: -7,675,904 bytes (-7.32 MiB).

2. build_files/cmake/platform/platform_win32.cmake (MSVC /Gy /OPT:REF /OPT:ICF):
   - Upstream already passes `/OPT:REF /OPT:ICF /INCREMENTAL:NO` via
     `PDB_INFO_OVERRIDE_LINKER_FLAGS` when `WITH_WINDOWS_RELEASE_PDB=ON`, and
     already passes `/Gy` for `MSVC_CLANG`, but omitted `/Gy` for standard
     MSVC `cl.exe` (preventing per-function dead-code stripping / COMDAT folding).
   - Add `/Gy` to `CMAKE_C_FLAGS_RELEASE`, `CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_RELEASE`,
     `CMAKE_C_FLAGS_MINSIZEREL`, and `CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_MINSIZEREL` when
     `NOT MSVC_CLANG`, and preserve `/OPT:REF /OPT:ICF /INCREMENTAL:NO` in
     `PDB_INFO_OVERRIDE_LINKER_FLAGS` even if `WITH_WINDOWS_RELEASE_PDB=OFF`.
   - `WITH_WINDOWS_RELEASE_PDB` remains ON so CI still produces `blender.pdb`
     for upload as a separate debug asset.
   - Exact `blender.exe` size reduction is unmeasured until Windows CI builds.

3. build_files/cmake/platform/platform_unix.cmake (GCC/Clang gc-sections):
   - Add `-ffunction-sections -fdata-sections` to Release/MinSizeRel C/C++
     flags and `-Wl,--gc-sections` to `PLATFORM_LINKFLAGS_RELEASE` for GNU and
     Clang compilers (when `NOT WITH_COMPILER_ASAN`).
   - Verified against GNU ld with `-Xlinker -export-dynamic` and
     `-Wl,--version-script=symbols_unix.map` that exported `Py*`/`_Py*`
     symbols remain GC roots while unreferenced local symbols are discarded.
   - Exact `blender` size reduction is unmeasured until Linux CI builds.

Paired workflow edits (staged separately in phase2-fix5-workflow-edits.diff):
- Linux: `strip --strip-unneeded` on explicit runtime ELF allow-list
  (`blender`, `5.2/python/bin/python3.13`, `libbf_intern_draco_bridge.so`,
  `libbf_intern_meshopt_bridge.so`, `libblender_cpu_check.so` — saving
  115,080,072 bytes / 109.75 MiB measured on fix4-linux, never touching
  prebuilt `.so`s or `libcycles_kernel_oneapi_aot.so`).
- Windows: package `blender.pdb` (140,316,672 bytes / 133.82 MiB) as a
  separate debug asset (`stephender-windows-x64-pdb.zip`) and exclude top-level
  `.pdb`/`.lib`/`.exp` and build-time host tools (`makesrna.exe`, `makesdna.exe`,
  `msgfmt.exe`, `datatoc.exe`, `shader_tool.exe`, `zstd_compress.exe`) from
  the main user zip (saving 165,810,154 bytes / 158.13 MiB on top of CMake's
  7.32 MiB Python PDB exclusion = 173,486,058 bytes / 165.45 MiB total).

